MGLRU backport host checks
=========================

Run from the repository root:

    python3 tools/testing/selftests/mglru/test_backport.py

HOSTCC (or --cc) selects a host C compiler. Python 3 and a C compiler are
required; no root, kernel module or running MGLRU kernel is needed.

The runner extracts clear_shadow_from_swap_cache() from mm/swap_state.c
and compiles it into shadow_model.c. The model provides sparse slots,
chunk-end next_index semantics, page/shadow sentinels and lock assertions.
It checks 2006 deterministic cases, including a hole beyond the requested
end, multiple entries in a chunk, swap-address-space boundaries, reversed
ranges, ULONG_MAX and seeded random sparse trees. The original donor
cleanup fails the range checks. Assertions are kept active at optimization.

This is deliberately NOT a kernel radix-tree, RCU, concurrency, page-table,
reclaim or device test. Source-guard checks supplement the range model but
do not prove the algorithm safe. See Documentation/vm/mglru-backport.rst.

For reproducing a historical cleanup regression, --swap-source may name a
file containing the old function, with --cleanup-only to skip source guards.
The test binary/source are created in a temporary directory and removed.
